---
description: Stack state model — MobX (mobx-react-lite) for client domain state, not server data
alwaysApply: false
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx}"
---

# Model (stack)

- Use MobX correctly and sparingly: `mobx-react-lite` `observer` only for components that read observable state; keep actions and computed derivations explicit.
- Don't mirror server state into observables — server data lives in the TanStack Query cache (see `stack/api`). Reserve MobX for genuine client domain state.
- Keep stores slice-scoped (feature/entity `model` segment); avoid global stores for what belongs to a feature (see `architecture/segments`).
